name,model,lines_per_mm,params,table_csv,reference
vbg_1800,bragg_kogelnik,1800,thickness_um=3000;dn=0.0005;slant_deg=0,,"volume Bragg grating typical of OptiGrate BragGrate reflecting-VBG product line (inorganic photo-thermo-refractive glass; catalog ranges: thickness 0.5-20mm, diffraction efficiency 3-99.7%, bandwidth 0.02-20nm depending on design); thickness_um=3000 (3mm) and dn=5e-4 are representative mid-catalog values for a 1800 l/mm (Lambda~555nm period) reflecting VBG, not a specific datasheet part number -- optigrate.com ; shop.amstechnologies.com/Reflecting-Volume-Bragg-Gratings/SW11876"
dammann_1x5,dammann,100,"transitions=0.03863,0.39084",,"1x5 equal-intensity binary-phase Dammann grating; two normalized phase-transition points (as fraction of grating period, in the first quadrant) from the standard tabulated Dammann-grating transition-point solutions for N=5 output orders (Dammann & Goertler, Opt. Commun. 3, 312 (1971), original method; transition-point tables for multiple N extended/tabulated by Krackhardt & Streibl, Opt. Commun. 74, 31 (1989)); lines_per_mm=100 is an illustrative carrier frequency, not tied to a specific catalog part"
ruled_600_table,table,600,,ruled_600_table.mietab,"measured-style s/p diffraction efficiency table modeled on Thorlabs GR25-0605 ruled reflective diffraction grating (600 lines/mm, 500nm blaze, blaze angle 8deg37', groove spacing 1.65um); Thorlabs' interactive efficiency-curve graph is not machine-fetchable, so the -1 order efficiency (peaking near the 500nm blaze, tapering toward 400/900nm) and suppressed 0th order are an engineering approximation of typical blazed-ruled-grating behavior, not a pixel digitization -- www.thorlabs.com/thorproduct.cfm?partnumber=GR25-0605"
lamellar_1200,lamellar,1200,depth_nm=18.3;duty_cycle=0.33,,"1200 l/mm laminar (lamellar) VLS grating, ALS 6.3.2 (Au-coated fused silica, 50-1000eV); depth/duty from SPIE 3150 comparison (partly search-synthesized); Underwood Gullikson et al. 1996 Rev. Sci. Instrum. 67 3372"
echelle_79,table,79,,echelle_79.mietab,"R2 echelle (blaze 63.4deg) 79 g/mm, Milton Roy/ESO; real ESO-measured 72%@500 71%@600/700nm anchors, rest interpolated; Dekker/D'Odorico/Fontana ESO Messenger 76 (1994)"
transmission_iof_cubes,table,3448,,transmission_iof_cubes.mietab,"Binary UV transmission grating (fused silica, ESO CUBES), Fraunhofer IOF; PTB-measured curve read off Fig.12 (approx); Zeitner et al. 2022 Exp. Astron. doi:10.1007/s10686-022-09840-1"
vph_eso_574,bragg_kogelnik,574,thickness_um=12;dn=0.02;slant_deg=0,,"transmission VPH grating (DCG, Ralcon/Wasatch for ESO), 574 l/mm, peak ~83-85%@500-520nm; slant ASSUMED 0; Rallison/Rallison/Dickson VPH Gratings for Telescopes (Wasatch Photonics)"
ruled_1200_500,table,1200,,ruled_1200_500.mietab,Thorlabs GR25-1205 ruled reflective 1200 g/mm 500nm blaze (17deg27'); efficiency engineering-approx anchored to 60-80%-at-blaze spec + ruled_600_table envelope; thorlabs.com GR25-1205
